// Cloudflare deploy config.
//
// This file exists so that neither the dashboard nor Wrangler has to guess what
// to publish. Without it, `wrangler deploy` runs its first-run setup wizard, and
// in a non-interactive build it silently accepts the default
// `assets.directory = "."` — which publishes the whole repository root,
// including .git/ and tests/, to the public site. That is not hypothetical: it
// is what happened, and .git/config was readable on the live site until this
// file landed.
//
// `assets.directory` must stay in step with build.sh, which stages the
// publishable site into _site/. CI asserts that it does.
{
  "name": "app",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-28",
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./_site"
  }
}
